#: ClassroomHost/MainWindow.Websites.cs
msgid ""
"Windows lets each user choose their own default browser, so Classroom Manager gives Windows a default for every user, which it applies when a user signs in: sign the students out and in again to see it. A computer that does not have the browser for all its users says so and is left as it is.\n"
"\n"
"The policies are written where Chrome, Edge and Firefox read their administrative policies, so the browser enforces them and shows \"managed by your organization\". Chrome only clears on close with sync switched off, so that is set with it. Firefox has no policy against new profiles; its profile page is closed instead. Firefox's translation is turned off through its Preferences policy, which replaces other preferences an administrator set there until it is restored.\n"
"\n"
"Clearing and removing cannot be undone. A removed profile loses its bookmarks, history and saved passwords. Firefox keeps bookmarks and history in one file: its bookmarks come back from Firefox's own daily backup, which can be a day old."
